<DocsLayout
  title="Manager App"
  description="Manage Ardor presets and assets from any browser, backed by the REST manager daemon on the pedal."
  lede="Editing on the touchscreen is quick, but a bigger screen helps for deep work. The manager app gives you drag-and-drop chain editing, asset management, and TONE3000 browsing."
>
  <h2>How it fits together</h2>
  <p>
    A REST daemon, <code>ardor-managerd</code>, runs on the pedal and manages
    <code>.nam</code>, <code>.wav</code>, and preset files — without doing management work
    inside the realtime audio process. Asset uploads queue a catalog refresh, and applying
    a saved slot queues a live engine swap that the pedal handles without restarting audio.
  </p>

  <h2>Three ways to connect</h2>
  <h3>Device-hosted browser UI</h3>
  <p>
    The daemon serves a built-in browser build of the manager from <code>/</code>. Open the
    pedal's address on your network and manage it from any browser — no install, and it
    keeps working without internet access because the bundle is embedded in the daemon.
  </p>

  <p>
    The manager provides bank/slot browsing, drag-and-drop chain editing, block validation
    and inspection, undo/redo, Save/Apply, asset upload/rename/delete, and light/dark
    themes. There is no desktop app to install.
  </p>

  <h3>Hosted control plane</h3>
  <p>
    An optional hosted control plane lets a claimed pedal be managed over HTTPS with account
    sessions, device presence, and physically confirmed claiming. Preset reads work over an
    authenticated connection; preset save/apply is opt-in per pedal and limited to a small
    set of allowlisted operations. The pedal's identity is an Ed25519 key stored locally.
  </p>

  <h2>Run the daemon locally</h2>
  <p>For local development you can run the daemon with authentication disabled:</p>
  <pre><code>cd services/managerd
ARDOR_API_AUTH=off \
ARDOR_DATA_ROOT=../.. \
ARDOR_API_BIND=127.0.0.1 \
ARDOR_API_PORT=8080 \
go run ./cmd/ardor-managerd</code></pre>
  <p>Then check the device status endpoint:</p>
  <pre><code>curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/device</code></pre>
  <div class="callout warn">
    <p>
      Authentication is enabled by default when no override is supplied. For a protected
      device, set <code>ARDOR_API_AUTH=on</code> and provide <code>ARDOR_API_TOKEN</code>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Assets you add here become available to the chain editor described in the
    <a href={url('/docs/ui-guide')}>UI &amp; Controls guide</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
